<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash soybeans down in moderate trade.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash soybeans down in moderate trade.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine cash grains and oils were little changed in quiet trading on the Buenos Aires Cereals Exchange Friday, with only maize prices showing gains of $1-2 a tonne.</p>
<p>Dealers said there were no changes in wheat prices and maize was only pushed up by the absence of sellers to meet buying pressure.</p>
<p>Cash soybeans were little changed to $2 firmer, mostly following gains in Chicago, and sunseed was unchanged.</p>
<p>(( -- Bueons Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
